# Level 5 → Level 6

## Concept
This level buries the password somewhere inside a big tree of 
subdirectories (`maybehere00` through `maybehere19`), each containing 
junk files. i actually did a manual view of directory sizes at first but that was my mistake then i realised that manually opening every folder isn't realistic, so this 
one's really testing whether you know how to search by file 
properties instead of just looking around blindly.

## Commands used
find -size 1033c
cd maybehere07
cat ./.file2

## Why it works
`find -size 1033c` searches the current directory tree for any file 
that's exactly 1033 bytes — since the target file has a specific known 
size, this narrows a huge pile of decoys down to one match instantly. 
Once `find` pointed to the right subdirectory, it was just a matter of 
moving into it and reading the file, which turned out to be a hidden 
file itself (starting with a dot).
